ubmissions are illustrated by new-product work, post-authorisation/registration work and specified reporting. The packet does not define when a submission is completed or accepted.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528","d19f9ecf9fd26.u17.2522"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"Existing channels are accepted during the parallel period, whose extension naturally carries that acceptance through 29 November 2024. No post-cutover exception for outages, pending cases or unfinished enhancements is stated. 'Where practicable' qualifies operational review and enhancement, not the mandatory submission route.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u3.737","d19f9ecf9fd26.u6.1187","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528","d19f9ecf9fd26.u10.2035"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"'Must' imposes the routing requirement. 'Will be integrated' describes system migration; 'can also settle' permits fee settlement through e-IP without expressly requiring that payment route. The selected control tests only submission routing.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The revised parallel period ends on 29 November 2024 and mandatory routing begins on 30 November 2024 inclusively. The earlier 29 October endpoint is superseded. The packet does not expressly resolve pending-case grandfathering or the controlling timestamp for a submission.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439","d19f9ecf9fd26.u3.737","d19f9ecf9fd26.u6.1187","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The earlier circular dated 8 July 2024 is referenced but not supplied. Dependency missing.4ad6b317ad4ade41b82f120a has no supplied text or source hash, so its content and relationship to that circular cannot be established. The packet supports the cutover rule but cannot resolve operational details or qualifications in omitted material.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does footnote 1 exhaustively delimit the covered investment products, or describe the products ordinarily administered by IPD?","Does the cutover apply to every submission event on or after 30 November 2024, including further material in cases opened through existing channels?","Which timestamp and completion criteria determine whether an item was submitted via e-IP?","What does dependency missing.4ad6b317ad4ade41b82f120a contain, and does the earlier 8 July 2024 circular supply relevant definitions or transitional qualifications?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The unit of evaluation is one application or submission event, not an institution's overall compliance.","The applicable date is the date of that event; the source does not establish the operational timestamp used to assign it.","The cutover applies to submission events in both new and existing cases; no express grandfathering is supplied.","Whether the relevant investment product is administered by IPD remains an externally supplied classification. The footnote informs that classification without an assumed exhaustive-list rule.","Extending the parallel run preserves the described acceptance of existing channels through its revised end date.","No omitted dependency is assumed to contain an exception, and no omitted exception is assumed absent as a matter of law."],"citations":[{"quote":"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u3.737"},{"quote":"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u6.1187"},{"quote":"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270"}],"distinction":"This proposed event-based reading makes the route mandatory for covered submission events from the cutover, including later submissions in existing cases. A case-opening interpretation could grandfather earlier cases, but the supplied text contains no express support sufficient to formalize that alternative. Similarly, mandatory submission routing does not make the separately permitted annual-fee payment route mandatory. The strongest uncertainty is whether omitted transitional material changes treatment of pending cases.","family":"time","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The evaluated event is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product; a standalone fee payment is not included merely because e-IP can process it.","name":"is_product_application_or_submission","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean classification of the evaluated event"},{"meaning":"The investment product concerned by the evaluated event is administered by IPD, with footnote 1 informing the classification.","name":"product_administered_by_ipd","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean classification of the relevant product"},{"meaning":"Gregorian date assigned to the evaluated application or submission event under the applicable submission-timing criteria; those criteria are not specified in the packet.","name":"submission_date","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The evaluated application or submission was submitted to IPD through e-IP; determining completed submission may require operational criteria absent from this packet.","name":"submitted_via_eip","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean routing outcome for the evaluated event"}],"result":"submitted_via_eip","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_product_application_or_submission product_administered_by_ipd (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))"},"local_id":"reading_1","questions":["Do omitted transition provisions grandfather any existing cases or particular reporting requests?","Are fee-related documents independently applications or submissions even where payment itself is optional through e-IP?","What evidence establishes a completed e-IP submission rather than a draft, upload attempt or rejected transmission?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] Selected control: mandatory e-IP routing for a covered submission event. Within the declared scope—an application or submission concerning an IPD-administered investment product dated on or after 30 November 2024—true means the event satisfies this routing requirement because it was submitted via e-IP; false means it fails this routing requirement. Outside that scope, this control gives no compliance verdict. Unknown inputs remain unknown. This is a proposed interpretation of routing alone.","subject":"Mandatory e-IP route after the extended parallel run"}]}},"run_id":"run.b85c4487afc44cd9861eb3f43d494627"}